BRepCheck_Face: the check of how a face's wires lie inside one another
(ClassifyWires) skips a pair of wires whose UV boxes do not meet, but gave
up the box of a wire (and so tested it against every other wire, a point
classification each) when the range of one of its edges reached past its
p-curve's own parameters. The edges of circles and ellipses of stored
bodies do so by a rounding error (an arc ending at 2*PI + 4e-15, or starting
at -1e-13), so a face with 2 929 circular holes classified 8.6 million
pairs of wires (3.5 s a face). A circle's or an ellipse's box is now that of
the conic over the edge's own range, whatever the range (the 2d box of a
conic takes any range); other curves keep the condition. The boxes only
skip pairs that cannot lie inside one another, so the statuses are
unchanged.
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepCheck/BRepCheck_Face.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepCheck/BRepCheck_Face.cxx
@@ -848,8 +848,15 @@
 
     const Geom2dAdaptor_Curve aCurveAdaptor(aPCurve);
     // IsInside() uses the original edge range, so a clamped box cannot safely reject the wire.
+    // A circle's or an ellipse's box is that of the conic over the edge's own range, whatever
+    // the range (an arc ending a rounding error past 2*PI, or starting just before 0, as
+    // edges of stored bodies do).
+    const GeomAbs_CurveType aType = aCurveAdaptor.GetType();
+    const bool              isConic = aType == GeomAbs_Circle || aType == GeomAbs_Ellipse;
     if (Precision::IsInfinite(aFirst) || Precision::IsInfinite(aLast)
-        || aFirst < aCurveAdaptor.FirstParameter() || aLast > aCurveAdaptor.LastParameter())
+        || (!isConic
+            && (aFirst < aCurveAdaptor.FirstParameter()
+                || aLast > aCurveAdaptor.LastParameter())))
     {
       return false;
     }
